column87:
"Exceptions" can be useful: lots of my code looks like<p><pre><code>    int fd = -1;
    char *buf = NULL
    if ((fd = open("/foo", O_RDONLY, 0)) == -1)
        goto err;
    if ((buf = malloc(1024)) == NULL)
        goto err;
    ...
    return 0;
    err:
    if (fd =! -1)
        close(fd);
    free(buf);
    return -1;</code></pre>
